{"_v":3,"id":"martin-guerre-west-end-2026","cat":"west-end","cs":68.97,"rc":10,"bd":{"positive":4,"mixed":6,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Claire Allfree","o":"The Telegraph","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/theatre/what-to-see/martin-guerre-old-vic-review/","d":"2026-10-21","q":"But lean into its pagan excess and heart-on-sleeve emoting, and this is a gripping evening."},{"cn":"Dominic Maxwell","o":"The Times (UK)","s":64,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.com/culture/theatre-dance/article/martin-guerre-is-too-confusing-to-be-another-les-mis-ld5pfrktp","d":"2026-10-21","q":"I’m glad I’ve seen Martin Guerre — but, definitive or not, I found it intriguing rather than devastating, skilful more than soulful."},{"cn":"Nick Curtis","o":"Evening Standard","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/martin-guerre-at-the-old-vic-b1301716.html","d":"2026-10-21","q":"Indeed, it plays out like a pacy, screamy folk-horror, but one that takes itself far too seriously."},{"cn":"Matthew Hemley","o":"The Stage","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/martin-guerre-review-old-vic-theatre-london-matthew-warchus","d":"2026-10-21","q":"What you’re left with is Leeds Mis, as a friend quipped."},{"cn":"Tim Bano","o":"Time Out London","s":56,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/london/theatre/martin-guerre-review","d":"2026-10-20","q":"But it is, simply, not a great musical."},{"cn":"Stuart King","o":"London Box Office","s":87,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.londonboxoffice.co.uk/news/post/martin-guerre-the-old-vic-review","d":"2026-10-21","q":"You betcha, without the tiniest soupçons of a doubt."},{"cn":"Alex Wood","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/news/martin-guerre-review-a-compelling-case-for-a-musical-with-a-complicated-past_1735581/","d":"2026-10-21","q":"This trimmed-down revival makes a compelling case for a long-misunderstood work."},{"cn":"Alexander Cohen","o":"BroadwayWorld","s":69,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.broadwayworld.com/westend/article/Review-MARTIN-GUERRE-The-Old-Vic-20261021","d":"2026-10-21","q":"There is a thrill to it as fingers point and tempers boil, but without breathing room for its characters, emotions are crammed down our throats. Though only Bertrande achieves three dimensionality, an impassionate Liv Andrusier 's performance is the production's anchor, but others are not so lucky."},{"cn":"Anya Ryan","o":"London Theatre","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/martin-guerre-review-old-vic","d":"2026-10-21","q":"And yet, it still doesn’t quite earn its place among the golden greats."},{"cn":"Michael Holland","o":"South London","s":89,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://southlondon.co.uk/area/southwark/review-martin-guerre-old-vic/","d":"2026-10-21","q":"The whole cast is fantastic; their voices are nothing short of angelic, and watching the play in the round really brings it all so very close."}],"au":{"score":79.16,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"ss":{"s":83,"c":75,"u":"https://www.show-score.com/uk/london/west-end-shows/martin-guerre"},"mz":{"s":75,"c":73,"sr":3.8},"ltd":{"s":88,"c":2,"sr":4.5},"sp":{"s":80,"c":40,"sr":4},"lb":{"s":72,"c":5,"sr":3.6}}},"cn":{"t":"This reworked Boublil and Schönberg musical shows improvement but still falls short of their Les Mis/Miss Saigon heights. Critics praise the production values and vocals yet find it emotionally distant and overwrought.","rc":9},"sh":{"wk":"20261026","days":[{"m":null,"e":"19:30"},{"m":"14:30","e":"19:30"},{"m":null,"e":"19:30"},{"m":"14:30","e":"19:30"},{"m":null,"e":"19:30"},{"m":"14:30","e":"19:30"},{"m":null,"e":null}]},"hi":"/images/shows/martin-guerre-west-end-2026/hero.webp","pd":"2026-10-01","ca":[{"n":"Liv Andrusier","r":"Bertrande"},{"n":"Mathew Craig","r":"Pierre"},{"n":"Dan Hand","r":"Young Martin"},{"n":"Bethan Louise Honer","r":"Young Bertrande"},{"n":"Alex James-Hatton